      "message": "Thanks, and sorry for the breakage. The time was not in line breaking. Under ASAN, TArray::emplace_back unpoisons and poisons the whole capacity on each call, so building the cluster table for 300000 clusters is quadratic. The timed layout(300) included that step. Line breaking itself took about 0.2 s of the roughly 7 s that I measured locally with ASAN. Your change in 1407716/1407560 (shape outside the timer, smaller input) fixes it. I checked that the test still fails in Debug+ASAN when the lookAhead change is reverted (about 23 s), so it still guards the regression. In the future, I will run time-bound tests in a Debug+ASAN build before upload.",
